cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: "AMIRA MCP Server"
abstract: >-
  A read-only Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for the Africa Multiple
  Interactive Research Atlas (AMIRA), the research-data platform of the
  Africa Multiple Cluster of Excellence at the University of Bayreuth.
  Built and maintained by the Cluster's Digital Research Environment (DRE),
  its digital infrastructure unit. The server exposes AMIRA's Omeka S
  metadata — research items, projects, research sections, people,
  institutions, groups, collections, the cluster bibliography with extracted
  full text, journals, podcast episodes and YouTube videos with searchable
  transcripts, plus the places, languages and subjects that connect them —
  as 26 typed tools that any MCP client can query. A complete data snapshot
  is bundled, so the server runs fully offline with no API key, account or
  VPN; when enabled it refreshes from the public Omeka S API. Every record
  carries an `amira_url`, so results can be cited as links back to the
  source. Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German
  Research Foundation) under Germany's Excellence Strategy — EXC 2052/1 —
  390713894.
